WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:07.800
[Ta-Nehisi Coates] If I injure you,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.433
the injury persists even after
I actually commit the act.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.130
If I stabbed you, you
may suffer complications

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.880
long after that initial, actual stabbing.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.620
That's the case with African-Americans.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.030
They're people well within

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.790
the living memory of this country,

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.218
they're still suffering from
the after effects of that.

00:00:27.498 --> 00:00:28.618
[demonstration leader] What do we want?

00:00:28.618 --> 00:00:29.688
Reparations!

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:30.866
[demonstration leader] When do we want?

00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:31.917
Now!

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.690
Reparations are meant to redress

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:43.690
or compensate for a really
egregious injustice.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:50.483
It can be compensation in terms of money.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.643
There also needs to be a moral reckoning.

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.020
The historical injustice
has never been addressed.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:02.220
Ending an injustice is not the same thing

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.143
as making up for its enduring effects.

00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:06.617
[Alderman Robin Rue Simmons] We need

00:01:06.617 --> 00:01:08.380
to have that controversial conversation

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.953
ongoing, so that we can begin
to do something about it.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:17.543
Repair is happening because we said, yes.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.760
A world shocked beyond belief,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:33.595
these are barbaric works
of the dying Nazi beasts.

00:01:33.595 --> 00:01:35.550
I'm originally from Germany.

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:36.899
And I grew up there.

00:01:36.899 --> 00:01:40.720
The Holocaust was discussed in
every single school subject,

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.720
and I felt horrible about my
history and ashamed of it.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:46.810
[inaudible 00:01:40]

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:49.500
the hideous handful who survived...

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.239
But then one day I met Mieciu Langer,

00:01:53.239 --> 00:01:55.730
a survivor of five concentration camps

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.443
and a death March in his youth.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.850
After he passed away, I
learned from his widow

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:06.407
that he had received a reparations
pension since the 1970s,

00:02:06.407 --> 00:02:08.540
first from the west German government.

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:11.630
then from the government
of reunited Germany.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.040
It was a small pension.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.350
It measured no way up to the
losses he had as a youngson.

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:19.940
There is no money amount
that could possibly

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.513
represent those losses.

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.860
When I came to the United
States, I was drawn to that topic

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.058
of reparations from my experience with

00:02:30.058 --> 00:02:31.720
Mieciu.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.370
The procedure that I use
to estimate reparations,

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.010
I took census information
about the enslaved population

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.520
in each year from 1776 to 1860.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.270
I'm adding up all the hours,

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.434
multiplying it with wages
customary at the time.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:51.140
And then adding a
conservative 3% interest.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.261
I arrive at a outstanding
debt of $20.3 trillion

00:02:55.261 --> 00:02:57.433
in 2021 dollars.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:01.737
We can see by the polls

00:03:01.737 --> 00:03:03.786
that support for reparations

00:03:03.786 --> 00:03:07.363
is over 70% among black Americans.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:11.861
A small but growing
number of white Americans

00:03:11.861 --> 00:03:13.962
also believe that reparations

00:03:13.962 --> 00:03:16.350
are due to African-Americans.

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.250
And I think that's an
important distinction.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:22.196
It's not a handout, it's a debt.

00:03:22.196 --> 00:03:23.029
No Justice!

00:03:23.029 --> 00:03:23.862
No Peace!

00:03:23.862 --> 00:03:24.871
No Justice!

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.704
No Peace!

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:26.537
No Justice!

00:03:26.537 --> 00:03:27.880
No Peace!

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:30.670
The advocates for reparations

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:33.100
explain in a heartbreaking way.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:38.100
You know, the systemic
ways in which blacks

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.100
and black families have been prevented

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.640
and held back from building up

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.650
the kind of generational wealth

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.250
that many white Americans can expect.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.270
I think reparations ask us to imagine

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.646
what America could be like

00:03:53.646 --> 00:03:55.560
without that kind of discrimination.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:59.280
As we begin to repair the
legacy of that discrimination,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.543
like what could America look like?

00:04:05.902 --> 00:04:07.740
[Alderman Robin Rue Simmons]
As an elected alderman here,

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.200
I serve my most immediate neighborhood,

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.280
which is the 5th ward,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.260
the historically black
community in Evanston.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.560
We are a small city.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:16.682
We're just north of Chicago.

00:04:16.682 --> 00:04:19.280
Aesthetically beautiful, mature trees.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.670
You know, the home of
Northwestern University.

00:04:21.670 --> 00:04:24.690
Majority white and majority affluent.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.910
The black community right
now is less than 17%.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.206
We had been in the
mid-twenty percents before,

00:04:32.206 --> 00:04:35.370
as, as early as 2010.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.810
So there've been an Exodus
in the black community.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:41.740
I saw that there were
historic and intentional

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:45.070
systemic barriers between black Evanston

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:48.060
in joining the same livability
as the rest of Evanston.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.130
And we were going along still
celebrating our diversity

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:54.270
and inclusion and, and that being a brand,

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.497
but still carrying year after
year, the racial separation.

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:01.380
Household income gap, the wealth gap,

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.363
the education gap, and so on.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.660
I didn't have the thought
to localize reparations

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.260
until February of 2019.

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.730
And it was in that moment,

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.930
that I immediately sent
out the initial email

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.190
to make the recommendation

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:23.766
to the Equity Empowerment Commission

00:05:23.766 --> 00:05:28.170
to begin the road to repair
in the city of Evanston.

00:05:28.170 --> 00:05:30.700
The local governments also have their own

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:34.030
specific, egregious acts
against the black community

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.600
that are verifiable and documented

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.230
and have measurable harms.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.700
So in my role as a local elected,

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.740
I thought that I might lead locally.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.090
You know, the frontline
is where your feet are.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.620
The first real grassroots

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.670
movement for reparations,

00:05:54.670 --> 00:05:57.480
that was led by a woman
named Callie House.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:58.830
It was in the 1890s,

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.630
and it was almost a two
decade long struggle for her.

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:06.630
And she made a claim to the
federal government for pensions.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:14.290
She used the mail to, to
communicate with Washington

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:18.140
and then also to encourage
people to join the movement.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:18.973
I know,

00:06:18.973 --> 00:06:22.070
at one point she had almost
300,000 people had signed up,

00:06:22.070 --> 00:06:26.510
were paying dues and the
government, in response,

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.500
accused her of using the mail for fraud.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:34.259
She was actually convicted
by an all white jury

00:06:34.259 --> 00:06:36.843
and spent a year in prison.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.150
Reparations for slavery

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:43.222
have been paid repeatedly in history,

00:06:43.222 --> 00:06:46.190
but to the wrong side,
to the slave owners,

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:48.640
rather than the enslaved.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:50.940
The French government
sent a fleet to Haiti

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.560
to demand reparations for the
abolition of slavery there.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.680
Similarly, the British
government paid reparations

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.030
to the enslavers in, in great Britain.

00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:04.320
In United States too,
reparations were paid

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.020
to slave owners in Washington DC.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.473
When slavery was abolished there in 1863,

00:07:10.403 --> 00:07:12.530
the recipients were white.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.550
It was considered normal,
and it's interesting

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:17.430
that the program becomes controversial

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.983
when the recipients are black.

00:07:21.531 --> 00:07:22.800
[Alderman Robin Rue
Simmons] Staff recommends

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.180
city council adoption
of resolution 126-R-19,

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:29.030
establishing the city of
Evanston Reparations Fund

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:31.543
and creating a revenue
source for the fund.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:36.473
So in 2019, we pass resolution 126-R-19,

00:07:36.473 --> 00:07:39.160
which restricted the
first ten million dollars

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.713
of cannabis sales tax to
fund reparations programing.

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:48.330
We selected that as a city
as our funding mechanism

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.770
because 71% of the marijuana arrests

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:51.940
were in the black community.

00:07:51.940 --> 00:07:53.080
And if you remember, I said,

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:56.390
we're only less than
17% of the population,

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.400
So certainly over-policing is an issue

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.120
and was an issue, in fact, then.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.410
So what more appropriate way

00:08:03.410 --> 00:08:05.793
than to use that tax revenue for repair.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.860
Eligibility is black
residents that lived here

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:12.670
between 1919 and 1969

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.410
and their direct descendants.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.752
And they will receive, if selected,

00:08:16.752 --> 00:08:20.620
a $25,000 direct benefit that can be used

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.080
for housing, to build wealth.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.780
They can use it to purchase a home.

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:28.790
It can be used to make any
type of home improvements,

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:32.943
but it has to be used to build
wealth through home equity.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:36.670
Evanston passed this program,

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.410
and now it is the first city in America

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:41.830
to begin a program of reparations.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.173
That is a pretty momentous occasion.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:50.460
It's gotten a lot of
attention, and you know,

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.578
it is showing a way, that,

00:08:52.578 --> 00:08:57.578
a city can repair harm
done to its citizens.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.700
Now, the program, initially, this $400,000

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.370
that will be given out in grants

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:10.370
of up to $25,000 will go to
probably about 16 families.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.780
I think the city council is aware

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:19.780
that it's a small, modest
program, and it's a first step.

00:09:20.127 --> 00:09:22.780
[public commenter] I am
confident that my four parents

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.680
and the many elders who raised me

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:27.540
and paved the way for me are rejoicing

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.720
because this is a move forward

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.530
for the nation and the world.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:34.380
Reparations, when you hear the term,

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.700
and as someone who's lived 18 generations

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:42.390
in one Parish and a Southern
state, this is not reparations.

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:45.860
A vote in support of
reparations programs is a sign

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:47.620
that my family is welcome here.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.610
It is a sign that Evanston
cares about families

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.900
that look like mine.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.370
It is an act of equity.

00:09:53.370 --> 00:09:57.467
When one is building a house,
one does not build a kitchen

00:09:57.467 --> 00:10:00.460
and then say, we will add other rooms

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:04.500
as we figure out what kind
of home we're going to build.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:06.990
It's just bad public policy.

00:10:06.990 --> 00:10:09.610
And it blatantly leaves an impression

00:10:09.610 --> 00:10:12.590
that black people are not
entitled to the same levels

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:16.503
of concern and care as other
city programs and projects.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:19.910
Reparations is a sensitive, you know,

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:24.110
very controversial topic
that gets at trauma

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:27.070
that the black community has suffered.

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:32.070
And a grant of $25,000
doesn't, to many people,

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.870
seem to even begin to really repair

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:39.333
that harm or acknowledge the damage.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.800
There is concern that, you know,

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.800
calling this reparations takes
away from this very big idea

00:10:48.048 --> 00:10:52.420
that the US federal government
needs to be responsible

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:56.800
for a very big program
that would benefit all

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.123
eligible black Americans.

00:11:00.177 --> 00:11:01.260
[Alder Robin Rue Simmons]
I had a colleague,

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.087
when I first began to discuss this in 2019

00:11:04.087 --> 00:11:08.380
recommend let's call it
anything other than reparations,

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:10.530
just to avoid the controversy.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:13.483
That made it very clear, we
needed to call it what it is,

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:19.275
but everyone in this process
is going to be uncomfortable.

00:11:19.275 --> 00:11:23.480
The black community, we
are renaming our injury,

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:24.863
and that's uncomfortable.

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:28.220
The white community, they're dealing

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.490
with their legacy of racism.

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:32.950
You know, if our ancestors
were enslaved, you know,

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:34.820
their ancestors were enslavers.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:37.260
And so those are
uncomfortable conversations

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.650
that we're having together as a community.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:43.530
And it's really been a
very productive experience

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.233
over the last couple of years.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:49.360
I've been appointed to serve
on the reparations committee,

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:52.220
so I will be looking at how do we increase

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.870
this initial ten million to,
you know, a hundred million

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:59.440
in the next few years,
and how do we expand

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:03.090
the work from a 10 year
goal to in perpetuity?

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.840
Because it'll take that long for us

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:08.563
to get to bridging our
racial divide in Evanston.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:13.550
I've been also appointed

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:17.350
to the national African-American
reparations commission,

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:19.790
and I will serve along
my colleagues there,

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:23.860
supporting other localities
and lending my voice

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.630
and advocacy to advance H.R. 40 as well.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:30.269
H.R. 40 is a resolution

00:12:30.269 --> 00:12:33.960
to study reparations.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.621
To look at what they
might mean in America,

00:12:37.621 --> 00:12:42.240
what they might cost, how
they might be structured.

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:46.420
It's a way to answer some of the important

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:50.220
and also sort of logistical
questions about reparations.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:51.720
Who would be eligible?

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:53.930
You know, what would a program look like,

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.703
and how would we pay for it?

00:12:58.197 --> 00:12:59.120
[President Joe Biden] Reparations means

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:02.500
making up for things that
happened in the past.

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:05.700
We should study reparations
and make a judgment,

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.700
what they should be, what they should do.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.767
There's certain things we already know.

00:13:09.767 --> 00:13:11.510
And I support that study.

00:13:11.510 --> 00:13:12.910
Let's see where it takes us.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:20.580
[Alder Robin Rue Simmons]
We have a president

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.750
who has said he supports
the study of reparations.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:26.560
The country has been awakened
and punched in the face

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:31.270
with our racism that we
experience far too often

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:34.159
through social streaming and other ways of

00:13:34.159 --> 00:13:36.523
public lynchings of black people.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:39.793
We are entering an era of repair.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:44.160
The Roman Catholic church
just made a commitment

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:46.780
to a hundred million
dollars for reparations.

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:49.580
There have been universities
that have done the same.

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.840
Corporations are beginning
to set aside dollars,

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.900
specifically not just for
our marginalized communities,

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:57.400
but the black community.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:14:01.283
Localities are doing the same
in advancing reparations.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:05.700
In Germany, 20 years

00:14:05.700 --> 00:14:07.340
after the reparations program,

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:10.060
the young generations ask
the older generations,

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.020
Where were you?

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.140
What did you do?

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:13.580
What happened in our city?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:14.850
In our town?

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.548
We have a situation where
we have street names,

00:14:17.548 --> 00:14:20.490
memorials and military bases

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:22.410
still named for Southern generals,

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:24.980
for the traitors in this country.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:26.530
But not enough for the people

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:28.400
that actually helped abolish slavery

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:31.090
and that put us on the
right track of history.

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.430
So I think there's a lot
that education can do.

00:14:33.430 --> 00:14:36.133
And a bottom-up process
would be fantastic.

00:14:39.254 --> 00:14:40.087
[Alder Robin Rue Simmons]
We're all learning

00:14:40.087 --> 00:14:41.490
and growing together.

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:44.950
We all aspire to repair the community,

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.600
and we're learning from our history,

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:49.100
but we have to take a first step

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:51.250
and we've taken our
first step in Evanston.

